            <ArticleTitle>Surgical treatment of coronary artery aneurysm after percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>217-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case of a 65-year-old man who developed a coronary artery aneurysm at the site of percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) in the proximal right coronary artery (RCA) is described. The coronary artery aneurysm was resected and a coronary artery bypass to the distal RCA was grafted to avert thromboembolism.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
